"Graph the ecliptic longitude against the days since the first reading for your {#} evenly spaced readings. Where on the graph is Mars moving east, and where west? From your stationary point readings, on what dates did the retrograde motion start and stop, and how many days did it last?",
"What was Mars’s elongation at opposition? Was the opposition near the middle of the retrograde motion or near one end? Using the view from above, explain in two or three sentences why Mars appears to move backward when Earth passes it.",
"On what date was Mars closest to Earth, and how does that compare with the date of opposition? Why do the two come close together?",
"Compare your measured synodic periods with the formula. Why are the synodic periods of Jupiter and Saturn only a little longer than one year, while Mars’s is more than two years?",
